# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers per path.
#
# Tier-5 AI-guardrail (see ARCHITECTURE_PLAN.md §1.3, §14): force a human
# review for changes that affect the bones of the template, where mistakes
# compound across every app spun up from this codebase.
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-configuration/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Order matters; the LAST matching pattern wins. Patterns are evaluated
# bottom-up by GitHub, so the catch-all is at the top.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                                @jessifoo

# Guardrail and CI configuration: anything that affects how AI code is
# allowed to land in this repo. Treat every change here with extra care.
/.github/                        @jessifoo
/scripts/verify-agent-toolchain.sh @jessifoo
/AGENTS.md                       @jessifoo
/CODE_STANDARDS.md               @jessifoo
/ARCHITECTURE_PLAN.md            @jessifoo
/CODE_REVIEW.md                  @jessifoo
/.cursor/rules/                  @jessifoo

# Backend lint / dependency policy: changing these effectively rewrites the
# rules every other PR is held to.
/backend/Cargo.toml              @jessifoo
/backend/Cargo.lock              @jessifoo
/backend/clippy.toml             @jessifoo
/backend/deny.toml               @jessifoo
/backend/rust-toolchain.toml     @jessifoo

# Frontend lint config — same reasoning as backend lint config.
/frontend/.eslintrc.json         @jessifoo
/frontend/tsconfig.json          @jessifoo
/frontend/package.json           @jessifoo
/frontend/package-lock.json      @jessifoo
